{#- The waitlist's form: one field and the call to action (targum-internal#69).

    A plain post to `/waitlist`, which answers with a page of its own, so it works with
    JavaScript off and from any page it stands on. Drawn on the landing twice and on
    every page in front of the door that sells (2026-09-27). `note` adds the line under
    it that says what happens next.

    The action carries the language the visitor pressed, so the answer, the mail and the
    invitation are in it (targum-internal#391). Where nothing was pressed the browser
    decides, at the post as it did on the page.

    `from` says which of targum's pages the form stands on (targum-internal#388): the
    page's `joined_from` where its renderer gives one, its canonical address where not.
    The server narrows either to a page it knows, and keeps nothing else.

    `link` is set where the form stands under the front page's box with a link tried in
    it (targum-internal#399), so joining keeps the link with the place.

    While the door is open (`door_is_open()`, design.md §12, 2026-11-10) the same one
    field signs up: it posts to `/signup`, which mails the sign-in link /account/signin
    would, and a tried link rides in it so Upload opens holding it once they are in. Under
    it then, where this install has a client, "or" and Continue with Google. -#}
<form class="join-form" method="post" action="{% if door_is_open() %}/signup{% else %}/waitlist{% endif %}{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}">
  <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ joined_from|default(canonical|default('')) }}">
  {%- if link|default('') %}
  <input type="hidden" name="link" value="{{ link }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <label class="field">
    <input type="email" name="email" required inputmode="email" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="email" placeholder="{{ t("landing.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.your-email", "Your email") }}">
    <button class="btn cta" type="submit">{% if door_is_open() %}{{ t("open-door.sign-up", "Sign up") }}{% else %}{{ t("landing.page.join-the-waitlist", "Join the waitlist") }}{% endif %}</button>
  </label>
  {#- Continue with Google under the field, only while the door is open and this install
      has a client (design.md §12, "Sign in with Google goes live", 2026-11-14). While it
      is shut the field joins the waitlist, and a Google press beside it could only be
      refused, so a shut front door draws no Google. An anchor, never a Google script. Not
      under a tried link either: the link rides `/signup`, and Google's `state` carries
      no link, so the popup that holds one keeps the one field. -#}
  {%- if door_is_open() and google_is_configured() and not link|default('') %}
  <p class="join-or">{{ t("signin.page.or", "or") }}</p>
  <a class="btn join-google" href="/account/google">{{ t("signin.page.continue-with-google", "Continue with Google") }}</a>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if note|default(false) and not door_is_open() %}
  <p class="join-note">{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-we-ll", "We’re opening in small groups. We’ll email you when your turn comes.") }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
</form>
